  ('zcrm_1579374000062687018', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000060442145', 'Suzanne Picard', NULL, 'Hi Kelly,

I hope you had a wonderful weekend.  I apologize for the lag in getting a response sent over to you on this last week!

We don''t typically work oncology related cases, as the chemo and radiation treatments can very rarely be negotiated.  It is also very difficult to pin point a "fair price", as the bulk of the price of these treatments comes from the type of chemo drug and the amount administered, which is specific to each patient.

I did find a price point that may be used for the "lumpectomy" procedure by searching CPT code 19301, which comes up on our website as "partial mastectomy".   If the member has been given a specific CPT code, she may also be able to search it on the website to pull more approximate pricing.  I was able to pull up facility listings and pricing for the lumpectomy procedure (based on code 19301) and the FP for this procedure is around $13,240.  There are also a few green facility listings that populate.  If the member is able to provide me with her specific code for the Lumpectomy, I can try my best to call to a few different facilities to obtain cash pay facility fee pricing on her behalf.  Even though we wouldn''t necessarily schedule it through BCC, I am up for helping with this however I can!

Thanks, Kelly!

-Jami Carswell-', 'Kelly Cheever', 'Kelly Cheever', '2021-01-25 10:43:17', '2021-01-25 10:43:17'),
