  ('zcrm_1579374000062131170', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000001696029', 'Keila Hoover', NULL, '1-11-21 She says both her dr. and PT are in the Anthem Pathway x Essentials network so we can move forward with the cheaper plan at around $83 a month with $20K income. But, she''s calling now to change her address from Arvada to Denver address. I just removed an even older Boulder address from CRM.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2021-01-11 16:20:18', '2021-01-11 16:20:18'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000062131162', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000055626044', 'James Young', NULL, '1-11-21 James called to login into CirrusMD bc he tested + twice for Covid from visiting friend''s house. Friend told him to obtain prescription for Ivermectin prophylactic which helped his friends fight it in a day! He hadn''t registered with CirrusMD yet and I got him through the process successfully. He was already in contact with a doctor by the time we disconnected! He was pleased.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2021-01-11 16:02:48', '2021-01-11 16:02:48'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000062131157', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000063253037', 'Bobbi Georgeton', NULL, '1-11-21 Bobbi is 52, turning 53 in March 2021, husband is turning 54 tomorrow 1/12/21 and daughter is 21 and DOB is 09/30/1999. Have Anthem now with Cobra at almost $1800 mo with $4K family ded.  Daughter is junior at CU and is still dependent. Husband learned he has an aortic bi-cusped valve discovered when applied for life insurance. He has to get is checked every 3-5 years and may need to do so again in about 1 year. Bobbi was in ER last week for high fever and low blood pressure. Thinks it might be from anti-anxiety meds Singulair. She also has degenerative arthritis in spine and celiac disease! They are not good clients for MCS. Daughter is on lexiprod for anti-anxiety as well. Bobbi wants to keep Dr. Jennifer Godberg who is showing up in network on Bright Health''s site. I told her to still double check with provider. Household income of $100K+.  Choosing Bright Health Silver $0 Ded/$17,100 Mop. About $1565.52. Need March 1st start date, so we have time. She will review it with her husband and call me when ready. We can enroll directly on Bright Health''s site bc no chance of income lowering below $100K.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2021-01-11 15:49:40', '2021-01-11 16:10:18'),
