  ('zcrm_1579374000061799026', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000060863094', 'Jenn Dempsey', NULL, '1-4-21 Jenn''s account is not showing her new enrollment other than on the initial overview page BEFORE I click on Manage account button. Then it disappears. Spoke with Cliff at C4HCO who was very helpful. He could see the plan was selected on 12-15-20 and then it was somehow cancelled on Dec. 23rd on their end. I confirmed Jenn did NOT cancel it by accident. The next issue is the doctor network changed as of July 1st, 2020 which cuts out UC Health and CU Medicine from the network which is what she needs. Cliff and I found articles - https://providernews.anthem.com/colorado/article/cu-health-plan-and-uchealth-changes-effective-july-1-2020 and information discussing the change. But, she kept seeing her docs through 2020 without problem. The network changed for Denver Metro clients. Perhaps Boulder is Not considered in the Denver Metro area, ie. therefore her docs are still included. I told her to call the UC Health Billing Dept again to verify if it will be considered in network or not. She needs a biopsy as soon as possible and doesn''t want to wait until Feb. 2021 to get it done if we have to choose another plan. I will wait until she calls them back again to let me know what she learns to move forward. Right now Cliff''s ticket will activate her Anthem HMO plans for Jan. 1st-31st 2021. Then we can choose another plan to start Feb. 1st. TKT # is 210104-001279. She''s super frustrated and nervous.  Told her they will backdate her membership to Jan. 1st. 2021.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2021-01-04 12:36:21', '2021-01-04 12:36:21'),
