  ('zcrm_1579374000061711038', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000022969020', 'Madisen Abbott', NULL, '12-31-20 Madisen called bc she thinks her income will be higher. It''s set at $22,200 now but her best guess is $35K possibly. She will be paid $17.30 per hr and the commission on top of that. Told her to keep it at $22K for now until it is more than 10% different than the $22,200 or she has a better sense of true income.  I mentioned CARE+ to her to help keep costs down, BUT she''s dealing with some health issues now. So, best to leave it alone. She also wants to keep her doctors. They are exploring why she''s having high blood pressure. They don''t know the cause and have done ultrasounds, blood tests, etc. They do not know root cause. She will call me when she''s more certain of income. When we put her income at $35K it brings her $237.75 APTC down to $20 APTC. So, her cost will be $261.04. Full cost is $281.04 for Bright Health Silver 5000 Rx Copay. Also taking and testing various meds.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2020-12-31 15:41:29', '2020-12-31 15:41:29'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000061711033', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000011521418', 'Joshua Keith', NULL, '12-31-20 Requested to cancel due to new employer group plan he''s joining.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2020-12-31 13:57:37', '2020-12-31 13:57:37'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000061711028', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000061768243', 'Haley Collins', NULL, '12-31-20 Haley 27 is Elizabeth Collins daughter. Haley is W2 FT employee for ortho office. She snowboards, hikes and golden retriever and hikes/walk with dog and boyfriend. No pre-x, no meds, no tobacco, healthy and rarely goes to Dr. Psyched for virtual healthcare since that''s what she thinks she will use the most. She enrolled in CARE+ for $1000/$215 Jan. 1st effective date. Makes about $32K per year. Super nice and happy to join easily.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2020-12-31 13:44:13', '2020-12-31 13:44:13'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000061711023', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000018451062', 'Patricia Bedell', NULL, 'Member left Bettie msg wanting to cancel plan.  I sent out link', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2020-12-31 13:08:16', '2020-12-31 13:08:16'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000061711018', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000044486166', 'Elizabeth Collins', NULL, '12-31-20 Liz called me back and said her card was on fraud hold for a day. She instructed Patti via email to run the card again. She forwarded me her proof of receipt showing the payment went through just fine on the 30th for $393. She won''t be checking emails until the 4th. So, calling her is best. Her daughter is interested in enrolling as well. She said to call her between 1:00-2:00 today to reach her. Liz was stressed since I sent her the old emails stating payment wasn''t received, since I didn''t know it was resolved. Looks like all set but Patti''s phone goes straight to vm today. Will try one more time.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2020-12-31 12:39:12', '2020-12-31 12:39:12'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000061711013', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000044486166', 'Elizabeth Collins', NULL, '12-31-20 I left Elizabeth a long vm to tell her how to update her payment with Concierge, me or online at MPB.Health. I will send her an email as well.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2020-12-31 12:18:46', '2020-12-31 12:18:46'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000061711008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000028294073', 'Amber Shipley', NULL, '12-31-20 With the VSP plan you will receive an ID card within 10 business days. If you would like to print an ID card for yourself or covered family members simply visit vsp.com to download card(s). An ID card is not required when visiting a VSP Choice provider, simply tell your VSP provider to verify benefits using birthdate and zip code, and are using the VSP Choice Network plan.
Please note:  While your VSP vision insurance is effective on the date noted above, your application may take up to five business days to be processed and be accessible in our system and through the network providers. For questions regarding your policy, or claims contact Ameritas at: 800-300-9566

