  ('zcrm_1579374000060923121', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000059893036', 'Stuart Brodkin', NULL, 'Member called in with questions about the Documentation upload for the Secure plan.  He will try to do it on his laptop and will let me know if he is unsuccessful.  He would like to change to bank draft.  I sent out link.', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2020-12-16 13:10:08', '2020-12-16 13:10:08'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000060946008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000061091292', 'Carl Cheetham', NULL, '12.16.20:  Carl emailed.  He checked out Zion and Planstin - noticed both companies have the same owner.  Ok with that.  Also noticed they offer Teledoc and we don''t. Asked why we offer a different virtual care.  Responded to his email explaining the benefits of CirrusMD over other telemedicine services.', 'Joan Phelps', 'Joan Phelps', '2020-12-16 13:10:00', '2020-12-16 13:10:00'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000060936023', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000060442360', 'Whitney Hammond', NULL, 'Member called and wanted more information about setting up an HSA account, I sent him all of the information I could find. - KC', 'Kelly Cheever', 'Kelly Cheever', '2020-12-16 12:54:26', '2020-12-16 12:54:26'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000060933079', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000026991181', 'Avery Dickens', NULL, '12-16-20 Avery is using wife''s insurance moving forward.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2020-12-16 12:52:04', '2020-12-16 12:52:04'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000060936018', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000011740011', 'Kathleen VanGoethem', NULL, 'Kathy called in very nervous and confused.  She hadn''t received any PDF cards from Zion or Planstin and never received a hard copy of the card.  She also wanted to make sure that everything on her post welcome call email was correct.  I explained that it was.  Andrea told her that she could not have an HSA with this plan, I explained that she could because she has a MEC.  I requested an update on cards from Zion/Planstin.....I was told that she is not in their system yet.  I let Patti know about this.  I will update Kathleen with what I was told about her cards.  - KC', 'Kelly Cheever', 'Kelly Cheever', '2020-12-16 12:48:43', '2020-12-16 12:48:43'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000060933074', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000025055122', 'Mark Wallman', NULL, '12-16-20 From cancellation form,  "Trying to get bills taken care of was taking too long and was requiring too much of my time having to contact the doctors and the hospitals for additional information. When the hospitals do not give me what I ask for I am the one that suffers because my bills are not getting taken care of. I do understand that you need this additional information in order to negotiate with them however this just does not work for me. I was able to get a policy from the marketplace that starts on 1/1/2021. Thank you for your help."', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2020-12-16 12:47:45', '2020-12-16 12:47:45'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000060933069', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000056191010', 'Beth Wilson', NULL, '12-16-20 Wendy,
I’ve weighed your suggestions—and I deeply appreciate them—and have decided to enroll in an Aetna plan subsidiary that is not in the marketplace.  I understand that Cigna automatically enrolled me. Can you assist me in getting out of it?  Thank you, Beth
I cancelled her plan just now for Cigna.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2020-12-16 12:22:00', '2020-12-16 12:22:00'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000060933064', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000060921716', 'Polly Tucker', NULL, '12-16-20 Polly is 54 and will turn 55 in March. She''s paying $700 to Anthem now and was getting $400 APTC which she might have to pay back in 2019 or 2020. She doesn''t want to have that moving forward. She made $49K in 2018 but about $20K more in 2019. So, Nelson recommended she speak with me. He''s been super happy with my help and with his membership. She used to be with Trinity Healthshare/Aliera which got shut down. Lives in Carbondales and new Dr. is Dr. Andrew Gisleson and he''s showing in the PHCS network! She has her own company and gets paid as W2 through her company and 1099 from all of her contractors/partners. She qualifies for SECURE $1000/$275. She was thrilled to learn of all benefits included in membership. She had a recent ER visit for fear of heart issue but it turned out to be an anxiety attack. She checked out clean and clear, no heart issues. She did have elevated blood pressure 199/145 at the time, but now it''s 135/90. She''s working on treating it naturally and has another appointment in a month to review her blood pressure to determine if needs to be put on meds. She had some crazy personal things happening in her life at the time which led to the ER visit. I sent a note to Tim Hirsch to see how they deem this scenario.
Chose to enroll in SECURE $1000/$275 for Jan. 1st start date. All set otherwise! Also contemplating cancelling accident policy that she thinks she''s paying $75 for a month which helped protect her with the $7500 ded Anthem plan. I told her she can likely cancel it or lower the amount to $3000 or lower.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2020-12-16 12:16:35', '2020-12-16 12:16:35'),
