  ('zcrm_1579374000060679038', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000060683010', 'Hilary Remacle', NULL, '12-11-20 Hilary called CU Sports Medicine again to verify who they accept and who they don''t. They don''t accept Cigna Connect plans, Bright Health or Oscar.  She called back again and learned they do accept Friday Health! So, she chose Friday Bronze HSA X Bronze/HMO $447.87. She''s all set for 2021. We also updated their income to show at least earning $125K via Michael''s investment income. Hilary is not working. We fixed C4 account that was showing they are on Cobra which they aren''t. They were on Cobra in 2019. I also removed all family members except Hilary to join a C4 plan. She will cancel her Bright Health Plan directly with Bright Health since we enrolled direct. She will also make sure to pay Friday Health in 7-10 days and set up auto pay.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2020-12-11 11:53:45', '2020-12-11 11:55:53'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000060679033', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000003748040', 'Natalie Lampert', NULL, '12-11-20 Talked with Natalie about why her membership is $30 more a month compared to her friend Brandi Stanley who joined per her referral later. Natalie''s membership has the special pre-x provision for immediate sharing of her Need. She does have an open need for her wrist that she still needs PT for. She''s working with her Case Manager at Sedera to get all of her records transferred to Zion. Zion has told her they are willing to waive the IUA if she can show proof of her costs submitted to Sedera! I asked her to keep me posted on this bc it''s even better than what I thought they would do. They aren''t requiring her to meet her $2500 IUA again with Zion. She says she had to put the first $2500 onto a cc and doesn''t have the money to pay another $2500. She''s paused her PT until she gets the information transferred and approved. I also explained to her the $2000 IUA was in error from Zion. Therefore, Brandi''s IUA will be increasing to $2500 from $2000 since Zion gave MPB wring information. Natalie also knows she can switch her membership in a year to the lower cost option if she chooses. Then her wrist scenario should be complete by then as well. Also SUPER appreciative of my help! She feels more comfortable with the move from Sedera to Zion with my help. She also shares this with many friends in part because of my assistance in making it easy and comfortable!', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2020-12-11 11:50:53', '2020-12-11 12:14:56'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000060679022', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000012379061', 'Lindsay Patterson', NULL, '12-11-20 Husband earns $400K per year so definitely not subsidy but we still enrolled through C4 since Anthem was more difficult to apply through judging from my experience yesterday with another client. Lindsay was SUPER appreciative of my help, professionalism, responsiveness over the years and it''s really allowed her to trust trying the new MCS options. She appreciates my help and guidance moving her daughter to traditional insurance to get them through the uncertainty of her daughter''s adenoid that might need to be removed.  All set and I told her to make sure she makes initial payment and ongoing payments directly with Anthem within 7-10 days from now.  She also said I have the patience of a saint!', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2020-12-11 11:24:52', '2020-12-11 11:57:44'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000060679014', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000012379061', 'Lindsay Patterson', NULL, '12-11-20 Lindsay is going to enroll her daughter in Anthem Bronze Pathway X HMO for HSA for $269.69. She did talk with Zion about her daughter''s adenoid and they finally told her they will pay up to $25K and possibly they would submit it to Special Needs case if something went wrong. But, she''s not super comfortable with that since they don''t really know what is wrong, no diagnosis yet. Therefore, playing it safe and enrolling in traditional insurance.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2020-12-11 11:15:27', '2020-12-11 11:17:12'),
