  ('zcrm_1579374000060516090', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000060863094', 'Jenn Dempsey', NULL, '12-8-20 Jenn called husband''s cardiologist and he got a glowing report. They are not worried about further issues with heart. Jenn IS worried about her recent breast cancer and she is also taking tomoxifin for 5 years now to avoid further problems. But, she understands the risk is too high if there''s a recurrence or if they deem anything new in another part of body as recurrence as well. Plus she''s had 7 basal cell carcinomas removed and did multiple MOHS surgeries. That is also too risky. So, she will go onto Anthem which I will look up for her Anthem Bronze Pathway X HSA.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2020-12-08 15:57:39', '2020-12-08 15:57:39'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000060516085', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000056191010', 'Beth Wilson', NULL, '12-8-20 Left her a vm regarding the above email. If she''s getting a C4HCO plan her agent likely won''t be certified to help her enroll in C4. If she goes outside of C4 she will NOT be eligible for reimbursement for APTC at tax time. So, she''s giving up that benefit. Just want to make sure she''s well aware of that.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2020-12-08 15:48:37', '2020-12-08 15:48:37'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000060516080', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000056191010', 'Beth Wilson', NULL, '12-8-20 Hello Wendy,
My apologies for a major change this late in the process but my former agent found a superior plan that better meets my needs. And she has recently received her licenses to operate in Colorado. So I’d like to work with her.
I am genuinely sorry about the sudden change. I do hope you understand. I appreciate all you have done for me during my initial arrival in Colorado.
Let me know what is needed to make the change and assign her as my agent. Thank you, Beth', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2020-12-08 15:47:16', '2020-12-08 15:47:16'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000060516070', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000060523080', 'Danna Hinz', NULL, '12-8-20 Danna and I enrolled directly on Friday Health. The system wasn''t accepting the exp date of the cc. I pressed the back button and it somehow submitted. It''s showing as such and it won''t allow me to do anything else. I told her to check on it and make sure her payment goes through by the 15th of Dec.  UPDATE - I went back in and we changed the payment to her bank account which worked. She''s all set. Payment conf # is 5846484584. App confirmation # 200056403_20201208160804. $428.79 Friday Bronze HSA.
Next we had to re-enroll David and child back into Worksite DPC with conversion group for $336/$1000 IUA.  Done! She also re-input the banking information for MPB to charge moving forward.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2020-12-08 14:48:04', '2020-12-08 14:48:04'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000060516065', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000060523080', 'Danna Hinz', NULL, '12-3-20 Danna and entire family are Nextera members with Dr. Flanagan. We are going to keep David and Shayna on MPB CareZ worksite membership for $336. Move Danna to Friday Health with Dr. Edward Donner for her back surgery. Might have to re-enroll to conversion to put David and Primary member. Danna will Friday $428.79 with HSA.  Let Patti know when re-enrolling to have John put product back up.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2020-12-08 14:47:55', '2020-12-08 14:47:55'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000060516060', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000060523080', 'Danna Hinz', NULL, '12-2-20 Danna is realtor and earned about $230K in 2020, so no APTC possible. She converted to Zion believing they didn''t have any pre-x. But, she has had back pain her whole life and there was nothing to do. BUT, she recently had tailbone/butt pain and it turns our to be crushed disc, exposed spinal cord and floating bones. She has spondelosis and 8" of movement and spinal cord not supported. Therefore, she can''t fall bc it could damage spinal cord. She needs 2 levels of a fusion completed and cost may be around $200K!  She will call Spine West and CO Spine Institute to ask which individual plans they accept and we will choose trad plan for Jan. 1st 2021.  She already had ultrasound and steroid injections and MRI''s counting towards her IUA. She is only protected up to $25K with Zion since she had chronic back pain previously. Traditional insurance will be best for 2021.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2020-12-08 14:47:39', '2020-12-08 14:47:39'),
