  ('zcrm_1579374000060183026', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000000689078', 'Kim Gangwish Zahorik', NULL, '12-2-20 Wants to auto renew. It looks like it might have done so already but I can''t see her enrollments. I will double check on Friday to see if account looks any different. 2021 shows up on home page accurately but can''t view in Enrollments yet. She is afraid of making changes now bc one family she knows lost 3 family members to covid! 2 grandparents and 1 uncle and now a 33 year old is sick too. If covid is managed by June she will revisit the MCS options and possibly include her company and other employees. Leaving her income alone at around $54K I believe. If income goes over $68K she will wind up paying whole amount back but hasn''t had any issues yet. She''s worried bc her personal income is different from her biz income which we never included. Personal income is super low and biz income above threshold. Accountant isn''t helping appropriately bc he hates ACA and doesn''t think she should use it.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2020-12-02 10:49:36', '2020-12-02 10:49:36'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000060183021', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000027993160', 'Karen Peirson', NULL, '-Spoke with Member regarding doing labs before the annual visit.  Told her most doctors like to see the patient prior to doing labs as well as needing a script written out beforehand is not the typical protocol for physician office.
-Member was instructed to call the physician''s office first and see what they suggest.
-I also told her I would look into a Walk-In Lab Clinic in her area and see if they can help her.
1:42:  sent text with link for a Walk-In Lab Clinic for her review.', 'Michele Rebal', 'Michele Rebal', '2020-12-02 10:44:50', '2020-12-02 11:43:28'),
