  ('zcrm_1579374000060172108', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000047153147', 'Tara Weaver', NULL, 'December pmt Declined 1st notice sent 11/30 Final Notice sent 12/2', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2020-12-02 09:13:21', '2020-12-02 09:13:21'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000060200008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000027993227', 'Catherine Young', NULL, 'Catherine Young called for some help because she thinks her kids have Covid.  I went over the gameplan in great detail- I sent her Sedera''s info on how much that they will share in the tests- as well as instructions on how to upload to Sedera''s portal.  I also went over the Spruce App- Redirect''s phone number and gave her an over all understanding on why this plan assists her the best when it comes to navigating medical cost sharing.  She seemed to feel better and thanked me for my help. - KC', 'Kelly Cheever', 'Kelly Cheever', '2020-12-02 09:12:28', '2020-12-02 09:12:28'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000060200003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000017830286', 'Maureen Gannon (Hanson)', NULL, 'from Natalie at Cirrus MD last night-
Hi Kelly,

Thanks so much for bringing this to our attention. I just got off the phone with Maureen and we discovered that she had downloaded the mobile app, which defaults to the Sign In page when you open it vs. Registration page. She was trying to sign in without having registered which was causing the issue. I resent her invite (we found it stuck in spam) and we got her registered and she is chatting with one of our doctors in the app now :) I also let her know that I would report this internally to our user experience team to see if we can re-work the flow of the mobile app to make the process more intuitive with the registration page being shown first or an option to register or sign in. 

Maureen, please follow up with me directly if you have any issues with your account access in the future and I''m happy to help further.

Take care,
Natalie

Customer Support', 'Kelly Cheever', 'Kelly Cheever', '2020-12-02 09:08:16', '2020-12-02 09:08:16'),
