  ('zcrm_1579374000060172078', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000008372009', 'Adrianne Middleton', NULL, '12-1-20 
Drug	Dosage	Frequency
Ivermectin	3mg	2 caps am & 1 cap pm
Bactrim (generic)	DS	1 cap 2x/day
Nystatin	500000U	2 caps 2x/day - except on M, W, F am
Fluconazole	150mg	1 cap am M, W, F
Itraconazole	100mg	2 caps 2x/day
Atovaquone/proguanil (MALARONE)	125mg/50mg	1 cap 2x/day
Ceftriaxone	150mg	1 cap 2/xday

The problem is that the plans don’t show which is a $10 copay and which is a $650 copay. And it makes a big difference. 

Thanks for the link to the plan finder. It tells me that switching from CIGNA gold to Anthem Gold is better, but it doesn’t tell me why. Anthem has a higher premium, higher deductible, and a higher out of pocket maximum. 
________________

Me - 
OK, I just researched the plans for you. I''d recommend staying with Cigna since it''s already a known success for you this year, I assume. If not, let me know. But, Anthem is more expensive and has a higher deductible and higher max out of pocket costs. Although it shows Bactum isn''t covered and one other medication isn''t covered on both Anthem and Cigna. The system shut down on me just now... UGH. Have you had success with each of these medications through Cigna?  If so, I would not switch. I don''t see any benefit of doing so. 

The only benefit of Anthem is if she takes any Preferred Brand drugs which is $70 co-pay or close to that instead of $100''s of dollars. I don''t know if any of her meds are Preferred Brand. If she likes her docs also, she should stay put.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2020-12-01 21:06:42', '2020-12-01 21:06:42'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000060172073', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000049242001', 'Madeleine Blanchard Cupolo', NULL, '12-1-20 I completed her enrollment after trying in many different ways. I got the system to work.  Chose Oscar Bronze Classic Next Bronze/EPO for $194.17. They have to make payment directly to Oscar moving forward.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2020-12-01 20:23:53', '2020-12-01 20:23:53'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000060172068', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000026335359', 'Benjamin Roth', NULL, '12-1-20 Ben was in a bad accident with a big fall. He went to ICU over the weekend. He''s now having a surgery today. It sounds like the situation is stabilizing. Katie and Ken Roth (Ben''s parents) are helping to follow the correct processes to submit the bills to Zion.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2020-12-01 18:10:22', '2020-12-01 18:10:22'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000060172063', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000000165320', 'Sherry Remick', NULL, '12-1-20 Chose Oscar for $414.51 with APTC of $292.26. Her cost is $122.25 with income set at $24K for 2020 and 2021. All set for Jan. 1st 2021.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2020-12-01 17:34:27', '2020-12-01 17:34:27'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000060172055', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000060442145', 'Suzanne Picard', NULL, '12-1-20 Suzanne 59, Steve 62, Eli 24 (independent now) Daughter is 20. Daughter had endometriosis 4-5 years ago and had surgery that most ins won''t cover. They paid a lot for it. She is taking birth control and not generic to keep it all under control. I told her that will cause it to be considered pre-x. Suzanne is taking HRT. She also had vertigo and ear infection recently. Steve broke his arm last winter and he has a plate and 8 screws. I told her all of this will be considered pre-x. They are using Freedom Life now and paying $1037 a month. Since son is independent he needs his own membership. He hasn''t gone to do wellness visits yet since super healthy. He can join CARE+ for $215/$1000 and they want SECURE for $685/$1000 for EF. They like the idea of setting up HSA for tax benefits and to help with hearing and dental costs as well. She will run it by her husband and we are talking on Friday to enroll for Jan. 1st. Teresa Robertson AND Adrienne Middleton recommended her to me. Teresa made the formal introduction and is a current MCS members. Adrienne is an ins. client.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2020-12-01 15:54:35', '2020-12-01 15:56:45'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000060179008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000057777111', 'Amy Chase', NULL, 'I really tried my best to help Amy understand her prescription benefits as well as her diagnostic lab work.  I really tried my best to explain the low cost lab options to her,  and tools to use in negotiating a price down on her own.  But it is my belief that she is so overwhelmed by all of the facets of the plan (she used the term "piece mailed")   that she can''t take any of it in.  I have reached out to Wendy about this member,  to brainstorm on what to be done.  I told Amy that Kelly F would do her prescription quote tomorrow, and I would get all of the info she needed for her labs. - KC', 'Kelly Cheever', 'Kelly Cheever', '2020-12-01 15:09:44', '2020-12-01 15:09:44'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000060172050', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000055626044', 'James Young', NULL, '12-1-20 James'' wife had ER visit to for fingers bleeding profusely for at least 20 min before needed to go to ER. It was Sunday night after hours. They were charged $1200 or can get a 20% discount to bring it down to $1000. Told him to try to get even more of a discount as self-pay patient. He will try since it''s highway robbery. Gave him the Concierge # to call to open a need.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2020-12-01 15:05:26', '2020-12-01 15:05:26'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000060183003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000034128172', 'Kim Delgado', NULL, '-Member called to find out if Covid testing was covered.  I told her it was an out of pocket expense.  She informed that a friend of hers who has the same plan went to a different facility and had been tested 5 times and they covered it every time.
-I attempted to do a three way with Apex to get clarification regarding this.  I had to leave a message with Jennifer.
-The member was giving Apex''s number as well to follow with her to get further clarification.
5:04pm - After speaking with Kellyanne - she gave me a document to send to her from Sedera stating they will partially cover it.  Document was sent.', 'Michele Rebal', 'Michele Rebal', '2020-12-01 14:48:13', '2020-12-01 15:05:30'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000060172045', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000074947065', 'Andrew Evans', NULL, '12-1-20 Andrew was referred by Jodi Ayers. He''s self-employed or rather employed by a 1 employee LLC he said. I''m not sure how he''s paid yet. He has Cobra benefits from former job. We are playing phone tag.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2020-12-01 14:44:57', '2020-12-08 12:48:39'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000060172032', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000056140001', 'Betsy Green', NULL, '12-1-20 Betsy was upset bc her dr. wouldn''t accept Planstin. I told her she needs to give them the card so they can see it''s the PHCS network. They won''t know of Planstin. She was relieved because she''s seen Dr. Sheila Bhagavan for the past 20 years. She said all of the other doctors are international/foreign docs and she won''t see them.  Dr. Bhagavan showed up in the network. She was pleased.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2020-12-01 14:30:33', '2020-12-01 14:32:00'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000060172027', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000011447234', 'Thomas McCarthy', NULL, '12-1-20 Left vm for Tom returning his call.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2020-12-01 14:20:38', '2020-12-01 14:20:38'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000060172019', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000056140001', 'Betsy Green', NULL, '12-1-20 Betsy called in to enroll not realizing she''s already enrolled. She''s separated/divorced from Quentin Green but I think he''s still paying for it. I will call her now. Left her a vm.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2020-12-01 14:14:31', '2020-12-01 14:16:04'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000060179003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000032809035', 'Michele Manna', NULL, 'spoke to Michele about preventative care protocol 30 min before her appointment.  Went through a whole crash course on it and sent her supporting emails. - KC', 'Kelly Cheever', 'Kelly Cheever', '2020-12-01 14:14:01', '2020-12-01 14:14:01'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000060172014', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000027993227', 'Catherine Young', NULL, '12-1-20 Struggling with Redirect a bit for getting them to respond in a timely fashion. She needs to be reimbursed for one PCP visit which they never got back to her about, so she paid. Daughter Brianna had a seizure for the first time ever while in CA and has since moved back to CO bc of pandemic. She had a visit with their family doctor to be allowed to get license back to drive again.  Told her to call Concierge Team to get the Extra Help link for issues with Redirect. She will do so.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2020-12-01 14:09:13', '2020-12-01 14:09:13'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000060176003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000060163052', 'Rita Boccuzzi', NULL, 'Member &amp; Ch $1000 IUA Secure', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2020-12-01 13:56:23', '2020-12-01 13:56:23'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000060144016', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000060863094', 'Jenn Dempsey', NULL, '12-1-20 Jenn is 54, husband, 54, and kids 21, 19, 15. They were on super great company insurance, then Cobra and now sees the terrible individual plans. She was on hold for 2 hrs. and 50 min yesterday and they told her the system was down and they couldn''t help her after that! Daughter is in school in DC. She has occasional basal cell carcinoma and had stage 1 breast cancer this year and had lumpectomy. She will call Dr. to see chances of it coming back. She doesn''t believe it can or will.  Husband had aortic aneurysm 5 years ago and sees cardiologist 1x per year for check up and all is well. He was born with bi-cusped valve instead of tri-cusped.  She understands the pre-x clause and she is going to call their doctors to determine the risk of recurrence for either of them. She loves the sound of this otherwise and is eager to move forward depending on the doctor''s response.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2020-12-01 11:28:51', '2020-12-01 13:31:29'),
