  ('zcrm_1579374000059783061', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000018419116', 'Judson Poling', NULL, '11-20-20 She chose to renew plan for 2021 for 8 months until she turns 65. I tried to update her income from $44K to $50K and that failed. But, I was able to renew her plan for Bright Health Silver  $3500 HSA with old APTC amount. She will just need to update it at a later date for 2021. It might have messed up Dec payment anyhow. The other plans were not HSA compliant and had much higher deductibles which she didn''t want. I told her to login later to complete her income change which will increase her cost by about $50 a month.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2020-11-20 17:03:05', '2020-11-20 17:03:05'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000059783050', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000060163125', 'Sharon Linnebur', NULL, '11-20-20 Sharon is turning 56 next month, 12/6/1964. She doesn''t have insurance now bc it was too expensive so she''s chosen to pay the penalty when it existed. Her income is about $47K which gives her a $490 APTC and $173.41 for cheapest Anthem plan or Silver $354.13.  I described CARE+ and SECURE to her. She''s thinking of doing CARE+ for this year and upgrading to SECURE next year possibly for wellness and HSA. She''s healthy, no pre-x, hasn''t been to drs. in years, no tobacco. She also plans to refer her kids 2 sons 27 and 28. Daughter is 23 and pregnant so needs to remain with plan until baby born. She understands that. She works for herself and is paid via 1099 and gets maintenance from x-husband. She''s probably going with CARE+ for $2000/$175.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2020-11-20 16:00:11', '2020-11-20 16:05:34'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000059783036', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000003176005', 'Jennifer Moen', NULL, '11-20-20 Jennifer found out for PT it''s $105 for first appt and then $85 for next visits. They have some openings right away so she can get started. But, she forgot to find out if insurance has co-pays for PT or if she''s working towards ded. If only ded then she can change for Dec. 1st. If co-pays then Jan. 1st start date makes most sense. She will call Anthem today or Monday and let me know what she learns after that to enroll.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2020-11-20 15:07:27', '2020-11-20 15:08:03'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000059790003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000005544245', 'Bethany Schaap', NULL, '45 min Welcome call complete!  I had to go pretty slow with Bethany, but I told her that''s ok!  I slacked Zion to ask if they had already sent out the hard copy of her card.  - KC', 'Kelly Cheever', 'Kelly Cheever', '2020-11-20 13:59:01', '2020-11-20 13:59:01'),
