  ('zcrm_1579374000059527013', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000066507053', 'Christian Knapp', NULL, '11-16-20 Julie 44, Christian 46 and two boys, oldest is 13 and other I am not sure.  Christian got let go from Aspen Skiing Company and Julie is furloughed from her job. Their full cost of current ins is $2600, but ASC paying all but $800 of it until April, then they are responsible for full cost. Mostly healthy. Julie had 1/2 thyroid taken out on Feb. 2020 to remove nodule. It was removed for cosmetic reason, fortunately nothing wrong otherwise. No more follow up appts for that moving forward. Also take lexipro and nuvaring. GoodRX prices are reasonable for generic. 13 year old has mild asthma and takes singulair sometimes, but never been to hospital and well manages. Christian takes finasteride for hair loss and generic is cheap as well. They want a Dec. 1st start date if move forward. Meeting again on Thursday with Christian to enroll.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2020-11-16 13:44:41', '2020-11-16 13:44:41'),
