  ('zcrm_1579374000058183021', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000001006052', 'Lauren Costantini', NULL, '10-14-20 I’d love to learn more about your current healthcare options. I recently left my startup and have severance and healthcare coverage (United health) through Dec 7, but after that am on my own.
I had Liberty for many years prior to this startup, but I saw the writing on the wall last year when their service plummeted, so I got the startup job (with United coverage) just in time! But may be back on my own soon.
Let me know if you have time for a phone call or Zoom Friday or next week.
Thanks so much,
Lauren', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2020-10-14 16:06:45', '2020-10-14 16:06:45'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000058183013', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000000165438', 'Gladys Diaz-Jourdain', NULL, '10-14-20 Spoke with Gladys and they are still with LHS. She will age out in June of 2021 and she has a number of issues she''s dealing with now. Just did IV therapy to boost her immune system which cost $1600. It''s called semocin or themocin alpha 1. She also fell and broke a bone in her foot and is doing PT. Also has muscle issue she''s been working on. Has shoulder and knee things going on. Not good to move her now. But, Ray is healthy, many years younger, no pre-x.  So, I explained a bit about our newest membership for $275/$1000 with MEC. He gets his annual wellness done every year. Talk with them in May of 2021.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2020-10-14 15:37:09', '2020-10-14 15:37:57'),
