  ('zcrm_1579374000058126003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000012535099', 'Shirley Ospina', NULL, 'Received a call from Shirley.  She was inquiring about her coverage and the options she has between ZCare and Sedera.  I spoke with her and told her I wanted to consult with home office for further clarification of her current plan.  I call Patti and ask her about Shirley''s plan and why Mike Leonetti changed his name to this account.  I am still the agent of record and still active with MPB.  I changed the account back to my name.', 'Ron Patterson', 'Ron Patterson', '2020-10-14 07:02:43', '2020-10-14 07:02:43'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000058097034', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000041152148', 'Justin Acker', NULL, '10-13-20 Justin called in to add wife and find out cost. I''m inquiring if we can add a family member to PSDHC or not. If not, we will explore the new options. Wife just turned 37 and no pre-x, no meds, no tobacco. Kids are all set on some other plan that is ACA compliant and wife is happy with. Justin is 42 now.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2020-10-13 15:51:06', '2020-10-13 15:51:46'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000058097029', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000025330254', 'Debra Rice', NULL, '10-13-20 Playing phone tag with her. Just left another vm.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2020-10-13 15:37:17', '2020-10-13 15:37:17'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000058097021', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000006644205', 'Martha Rybak', NULL, '9-13-20 Martha is still trying to understand and decide what membership is best for LHS conversion. She was originally diagnosed with staf infection and then later with shingles. Shingles seems to be the accurate diagnosis. So, I need to make sure she''s with Redirect or a conversion option to tend to any pre-x if necessary. Knows of the 20th of the month deadline.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2020-10-13 15:33:37', '2020-10-13 15:33:49'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000058097013', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000026023246', 'Kristy Barber', NULL, '10-13-20 Kristy called bc the PHCS network has been a challenge to work with. She had annual visit and blood work. Then doctor wanted a follow up visit to go over blood work. She had to pay for the follow up visit.  She is just getting bills now from 1 year ago. One is for dermatology visit- skin check for $130 and she paid that already since not included.  I let her know both of these challenges will be the same with traditional insurance since the inclusions are dictated by the ACA and one annual wellness visit per year. 

She just received some other bills for heart scare that turned out to be nothing. Few tests and doctor visits that will exceed $500 easily. One is for $3000. She previously called the doctor to pay the bills a while back and they told her they were simply behind in billing and didn''t give her a bill. She knows how to create a Need. She will do that now with the bills she has, but she''s expecting more. This is the first time she''s receiving a bill even though the dates of service started in June of 2019. I recommended to make it clear this is the first bill she received and she''s uploading it immediately.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2020-10-13 15:15:34', '2020-10-13 15:18:16'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000058102021', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000058081094', 'Beth White-OConnor', NULL, 'Member Only $1000 60-64 Care Plus - Sedera', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2020-10-13 13:48:17', '2020-10-13 13:48:17'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000058109003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000008282039', 'Melissa Harper', NULL, 'Melissa called in and said she had her welcome call with Vanessa and she called Planstin to make sure the person she found in the PHCS network was in network and just make sure she was doing the right thing and Cat with Planstin told her with her type of plan that Mammograms and Colonoscopies are NOT covered with her plan guidelines. I told her I will figure this out and call her back. I have never heard of that before of those things not being something that is covered. I called Planstin and actually spoke to the same lady Cat and she said yes with her plan they are not. I told her I have never heard that before and really was pushing her to make sure. She said hold on and put me on hold for a minute and then came back and deeply apologized and said she gave her misinformation and those 2 items as long as they are just the regular screening (which Melissa said that is all she wants for her Mammogram) they ARE covered. I told her it is no problem, people do it all the time. I called Melissa back to let her know the good news and she was very happy and said its not issue and will continue with making her appointment for her annual Mammogram screening. All set. -KF', 'Kelly Frederickson', 'Kelly Frederickson', '2020-10-13 13:25:27', '2020-10-13 13:25:27'),
