  ('zcrm_1579374000056987103', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000017033139', 'Kim Rew', NULL, 'Sent Refund Explanation Letter', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2020-09-15 13:38:00', '2020-09-15 13:38:00'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000057021028', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000011716907', 'Joleen Gerber', NULL, 'Joleen called in and said this will be the first time she is going to need to make a claim. She thinks she broke both of her ankles/feet and wanted to know what to do. I explained everything that she needs to do with presenting herself as a cash pay patient and showing her Zion card, which she said she does have. I let her know she is only responsible for $1000 of her IUA and anything after that she is to ask to be billed the rest and then start a need with Zion. I told her to call Zion when she gets off the phone with me and just let them know what is going on and they can walk her through the process of what she needs to do. She also asked if we have a list of preferred places to go or providers. I told her I can certainly look up a few providers for her in her area and give her the links to their profile to see all their reviews and I cross referenced them with HCBB to see what their rating was for cost. I gave her 3 providers from healthgrades.com and there were a LOT of 5 star reviews that were in her area and most of them were amazing reviews and low cost. Also the first provider I gave her specializes in broken ankle/feet. All of the providers were specifically for broken bones. She thanked me greatly and will take a look when she gets it and go wherever she is going to choose asap to get x-rays done. -KF', 'Kelly Frederickson', 'Kelly Frederickson', '2020-09-15 13:25:47', '2020-09-15 13:25:47'),
