  ('zcrm_1579374000056846003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000028466180', 'Sarah Pyper', NULL, 'Cust. Service Issue
Posted by Jane Kassel on 3/13/2020 at 4:48 PM Mountain Standard Time
Another issue - this time her Well Check
Email from Sarah:

Please have the Re Direct person call me

Sarah Pyper
2:29 PM (1 hour ago)
to me

I am sorry to have to constantly bother you but yet again I am having a problem.
I contacted Re Direct to set up my mammogram. They contacted Simon Med on camelback and 68 street . Simon Med called me right away and set an appointment for me today. I arrived at 1:50, filled out my paperwork, and they asked for my insurance card. I let them know that this was arranged by Re Direct and that it was paid. They insisted it wasn''t and I would need to pay. I called Re direct and after a long hold while the gentleman was trying to figure out what was going on, he said that it had been paid on March 6. He asked to speak to the person at the desk and she refused.
I have never had so much hassle for health care. I am very very upset. I have no idea what I am paying $350 per month for. The service is terrible and I feel like I am a homeless person begging for minimal healthcare through the county.
Sarah
---
From Kevin Fechtmeyer:
Looks like direct health is the culprit - they''ve missed almost everyone of Sarah''s appt - she was again turned away from an appt they set up for a mammogram - they are perfectly teed up for a lawsuit.
Kevin', 'Jane Kassel', 'Jane Kassel', '2020-09-09 10:55:45', '2020-09-09 10:55:45'),
