  ('zcrm_1579374000056611003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000056599004', 'Adam Davis', NULL, 'Member Only $1000 IUA MPB CareZ  Wkst +MEC', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2020-09-02 09:41:39', '2020-09-02 09:41:39'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000056596008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000010656193', 'Char Moe', NULL, 'Char called in today and said that she has an appointment TODAY with her OBGYN and does not have any of her cards. The type of appointment is a follow up from a scan that she had. I told her that she would be a cash pay patient up to her IUA of $1000 and she said that they are still going to ask for her "Insurance Card" and number. I told her that she will need to call Zion and gave her their number. When I mentioned this to Patti and Michele and they asked what her start date is. She started 9/1/20 so she is not going to have any cards or be in their system yet because she literally just started yesterday and won''t have any cards or anything until around the 11th-15th of the month. If she calls back in I will explain this to her and the only thing that can be done is to ask her to reschedule her appointment until she has her cards and info that she needs. -KF', 'Kelly Frederickson', 'Kelly Frederickson', '2020-09-02 09:41:19', '2020-09-02 09:41:19'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000056602003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000011521288', 'Robert Glowczewsky', NULL, '- Member called in wanting the Provider Network Search link.
- Provider Network Search Template with link was sent  - MR', 'Michele Rebal', 'Michele Rebal', '2020-09-02 09:13:30', '2020-09-02 09:13:30'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000056596003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000006871163', 'Deborah Pettit', NULL, 'Deborah called in and just wanted to make sure that her and her husband were doing the right thing when it comes to their annual wellness visit. I looked up the provider and they are in the PHCS Network and explained how everything has to be preventative only and the billing has to be coded as such. I told her to make sure she brings her RCI card and explained the phone number on the back that they will call to verify benefits and the P.O. Box address that all billing must be submitted to RCI. I sent her the email that explains how she will present her card. I also checked to make sure the facility she is going to for her mammogram is also in the PHCS Network and it is. She is all set and understood everything that she has to do. -KF', 'Kelly Frederickson', 'Kelly Frederickson', '2020-09-02 09:07:37', '2020-09-02 09:07:37'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000056578003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000035605393', 'Ian McLendon', NULL, 'Addition of Etta/spouse:
Tracking #10494407
Sent by Patti Baron on 9/2/2020', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2020-09-02 08:32:49', '2020-09-02 08:32:49'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000056551118', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000028471248', 'Charles Christian Figge VI', NULL, '9-1-20 Figge has an Open Need with Sedera that he wants to finish caring for with PT with Spine West in Boulder.  His need has been opened since Aug. of 2019 and he needs to see a physio therapist which was prescribed to him in Feb. 2020. He wasn''t able to follow through bc of covid. He now wants to follow through. He didn''t understand the change would be mean he''d have to start a Need over again.  He and I never talked. His assistant Anna Thexton and I played serious phone tag. We never talked. She helped him make the decision without understanding that he''d have to start a new Need with Zion to finish up his back issue. He''d like to switch back if at all possible. He also has adult ADD he needs to treat but both memberships are super limited. I read the Guidelines for each company to him to help him decide. Either way, it''s likely just going to be meds to handle his ADD and may not ever meet the IUA. So, best case scenario he remains with Sedera to close out his need to see the physio therapist for $85 per visit. He''s self employed and super stressed and struggles with all of this admittedly.  He just wants help and doesn''t have a lot of money to deal with any of this. Income is likely around $60K or $45K worst case, not low enough for great subsidy.  If we can out him on Sedera Access Plus, that would be best case scenario for him at this point.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2020-09-01 17:16:21', '2020-09-01 17:45:54'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000056551113', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000039755139', 'Shelley Scipione', NULL, '9-1-20 Congratulations, you have just enrolled in the consumer’s #1 choice in vision care*. Here is what you need to know:

Do not respond to this confirmation email. Please allow 5-7 business days for your application to be processed. For questions regarding your policy, you may contact your plan administrator at 800.487.5553 or by email at: spirit@ameritas.com.

• 	With the VSP plan you will receive an ID card within 10 business days. If you would like to print an ID card for yourself or covered family members simply visit vsp.com to download card(s). An ID card is not required when visiting a VSP Choice provider, simply tell your VSP provider to verify benefits using birthdate and zip code, and are using the VSP Choice Network plan.
Please note:  While your VSP vision insurance is effective on the date noted above, your application may take up to five business days to be processed and be accessible in our system and through the network providers. For questions regarding your policy, or claims contact Ameritas at: 800-300-9566

Provider must verify benefits using birthdate and zip code.
    For Claims, Contact VSP: 800-877-7195
Find VSP Providers at VSP.com (Choose the Choice + Affiliates Network)
        Customer Service (other than claims), Contact Ameritas: 866-619-6095
    Enrollment or Payment Questions: spirit@ameritas.com
Per your enrollment, your specific coverage information is as follows:
    
    Confirmation Number:   320004164
    Plan Selected:   VSP Plan A + Vision
    Coverage Level:   Individual
    Effective Date:   09/02/2020
    Zip Code:   80302
    Vision Monthly Premium:   $15.97
    Agent Info:   Wendy Scipione - (720) 259-1555

Payment Information:
1. Initial premium will be withdrawn within 3 days of your policies effective date, subsequent premiums are due on the day of the month in which the policy was effective.
2. Plan includes a one-time non-refundable enrollment fee of $25. This charge will be made at the time of purchase and may appear as a separate transaction from your insurance as Spirt Dental or Direct Benefits, Inc.

Questions? Call 844-833-8440 or chat with us at DirectVisionInsurance.com', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2020-09-01 16:53:15', '2020-09-01 16:53:15'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000056551108', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000005568047', 'Paige Payne', NULL, '9-1-20 Unsubscribe requested and I selected Opt Out.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2020-09-01 16:51:44', '2020-09-01 16:51:44'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000056551103', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000000191497', 'Michael Rust', NULL, '9-1-20 Wendy,

Thanks for the information.  We too have experienced long delays from Liberty in paying medical bills.  In most instances we are forced to pay the medical bills so it does not impact our credit negatively.  We are still waiting to be reimbursed from Liberty for things in 2019.  While this is indeed frustrating, the "changemyliberty" still has too many restrictions on preexisting conditions of which all of Michael''s issues are preexisting.  We have decided to stick with Liberty at this time.

Thanks so much!', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2020-09-01 16:48:55', '2020-09-01 16:48:55'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000056551098', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000028471248', 'Charles Christian Figge VI', NULL, '9-1-20 Call him Figge. He''s asking about dental options. He might have a cavity. He''s also looking for a new dentist. I told him about Dr. Alber and the membership with Dr. Alber and 15% discount and free cleanings, no insurance to deal with. He lives in Louisville.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2020-09-01 16:46:29', '2020-09-01 16:46:29'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000056551093', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000001176011', 'Shannon Rahlves', NULL, '9-1-20 Shannon''s gall bladder removal was Nov. 2017 and appendix was Feb. 2018. So, out of pre-x time frame. I still explained the pre-x clause thoroughly in case there''s anything else on her record. She''s changed her diet since then as well. Super athlete and is done with doctors other than gyn for annual wellness, etc.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2020-09-01 16:32:08', '2020-09-01 16:32:08'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000056551088', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000006176111', 'Lisa Carnahan', NULL, '9-1-20 Lisa enrolled in MPB Care Connected Worksite NO DPC for $317/$1000. All set.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2020-09-01 16:02:08', '2020-09-01 16:02:08'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000056551083', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000108399027', 'Doris Medina', NULL, '9-1-20 From Reid "We cannot do anything for the Oxygen tank but it looks like they are doing better than I can offer for the other 2. I will quote the Breo and Levothyroxine below for reference.

