  ('zcrm_1579374000055966003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000005630587', 'Lisa Eden', NULL, 'Lisa,

  Nice hearing back from you.  Below, is the link to convert to MPB CareZ.  However, to be upfront with you; I am not aware of Liberty’s policy on paying an open claim if you cancel before they payout to you.  You may want to call and ask them prior to switching.  I certainly don’t want you to be left in a lurch should you switch beforehand.  Also, if your fiancé was diagnosed for anxiety that would be a pre-existing condition and would not be eligible for sharing for a year.  Click on the link and follow the prompts, once you feel comfortable in proceeding.  Should you have further questions or clarification, please feel to reach out to me via my contact information.

https://myahe.clickfunnels.com/liberty-conversion41996199


Hope all is well,  


____________________________

Michael Leonetti
ICHRA Advisor
MPowering Benefits/MPB.Health
800.519.2969
954.328.3625
www.MPB.Health
 


From: Lisa Eden <lisajoeden@gmail.com> 
Sent: Friday, August 21, 2020 3:36 PM
To: Michael Leonetti <mikel@mympb.com>
Subject: Info needed

Hi Mike,

We spoke this morning about me and my fiancé switching over to you from our Liberty Healthshare accounts to your company.  Please send me info on how to do this.  My fiancé does have an open claim at the moment that has been submitted to Liberty so I’m wondering what happens if we switch before we see payment.  He had to go to the ER a couple weeks ago, had chest pain and after testing his vitals, blood and EKG it was determined to be anxiety.  He followed up with his regular doc and the bill from the ER has been sent to Liberty.  So what happens if he switches now?

Thank you for any info you can provide we are very interested in your company!

Regards,', 'Michael Leonetti', 'Michael Leonetti', '2020-08-21 13:58:51', '2020-08-21 13:58:51'),
