  ('zcrm_1579374000055742039', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000021624144', 'Kim Merryweather', NULL, '8-19-20 Kimberly had a colonoscopy back in March and then also did an EDG (through the throat) and learned she has mild gurd and barrett''s( disease?).  She has no need to go back for another 3 years. She is going to the dentist on Monday and was wondering if the gurd and barrett''s caused problems with her teeth if it would be shareable. Judging from the guidelines it sounds like the answer is no. Then she asked about vision. She has an eye appt coming up and wants to know if she needs cataract surgery if that''s included. Zion answered on the Chat that they would share this as a Special Needs and handled on a case per case basis if the sharing funds are available. Kimberly said just using that as an example. She''s bummed bc dental and vision aren''t necessarily included even if really a medical issue. She was most concerned with her next appointment in 3 years for the follow up that she wanted shared. I need to let her know she''d still repay her IUA even with Sedera in 3 years.  She will choose MPB Carez with MEC for $344/$1000. Scheduled to complete tomorrow.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2020-08-19 12:20:59', '2020-08-19 13:13:36'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000055723151', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000008640041', 'Allison Adams', NULL, 'helped Allison via SalesIQ complete her conversion form. - KC', 'Kelly Cheever', 'Kelly Cheever', '2020-08-19 11:49:41', '2020-08-19 11:49:41'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000055723146', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000011779188', 'Jason LaPointe', NULL, 'I ran a search for Wendy for Mammogram, also I called her to let her know that the information she had gotten a little over a week ago wasn''t correct, that she didn''t have ASI any longer and that she shouldn''t expect Planstin to cover up to 130% Medicare allowable as ASI did.  I told her that if it is out of network...it won''t be covered. - KC', 'Kelly Cheever', 'Kelly Cheever', '2020-08-19 11:41:11', '2020-08-19 11:41:11'),
